## Recall Landscape Analysis

As of now, 2026 has seen 327 recalls in total, with Class I hazards--those presenting serious health risks--accounting for 90 of them. The latest batch brings a diverse mix of issues, with undeclared allergens taking center stage.

## A Surge in Undeclared Allergens

Recent recalls include products by industry giants Costco and Mondelez. Costco's Kirkland Signature Madeleines were flagged for undeclared hazelnut and soy lecithin, a Class I concern that raises alarms for those with allergies. Mondelez's Chips Ahoy! Baked Bites Brookie displayed hard corn starch lumps, a physical defect. These incidents highlight the importance of vigilance on both manufacturing and consumer fronts.

## Notable Repeat Offenders

Brands like CHETAK NEW YORK LLC and Diva Fam Inc continue to populate the recall lists, with the former maintaining a concerning history of Class I violations.

## A Warning to Consumers

Several products contained undeclared ingredients, including Bombay Kitchen's snack lines. This trend underscores the need for transparency and robust labeling from manufacturers.

## Brands to Watch

The report highlights Moonlight Packing Corporation and Albertsons Companies LLC as top offenders in 2026 so far. Both have numerous recalls and Class I violations, demanding scrutiny.

## Conclusion

Stay informed and cautious. Check labels meticulously, and stay updated on recall notices. Your health may very well depend on it.
